			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1366538">
									

<p>Sorry to say that, but current version of the object is really worse than it was earlier. Too much unnecessary details, odd calculations and &quot;████████&quot;. And, of course, some moments in text made me cry:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We ask that future team members with access to the chamber keep their hands clear of SCP-090.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I imagine: new team members suddenly break into 090 contaiment cell after the midnight just to grope or play with a Keter class object. How unprofessional. If that's so, they're kids, not Foundation staff.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>████████ was eliminated and his/her assets seized by the facility at the time of acquisition.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Guess, &quot;seized by Foundation&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;The request for a predictive supercomputer (████████) has been placed on hold indefinitely, so all data parsing is currently under jurisdiction of ████████ personal computer&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My 343, Foundation is too slow (or too greedy), to provide a supercomputer for a Keter. Sounds like 090 is not a Keter and just causes uncontrollable flatulence in exposed personnel with every object's realignment.</p>
<p>Downvoted, until all this weak places will be fixed.</p>

